course: dictionary
lesson: 14143
title: Misdeed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A misdeed is a wrong or bad action. The word has two parts: mis- means wrong, and deed means something a person does. So a misdeed is a wrong deed. «The thief was caught after many misdeeds.» The word thief is a clue: a thief does bad things, so misdeeds must mean bad actions.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Sam owned up to his misdeed and said sorry.» Owning up means admitting what you did, and saying sorry is what you do after something wrong. So a misdeed is something you have done that was wrong.
explain: Misdeed is a formal word, so you will often meet it in stories and history books. Check by swapping in "wrong action": if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A misdeed is a wrong or bad action, especially a crime or a breaking of rules.
fact: Mis- means wrong, and deed means an action, so a misdeed is a wrong action.
fact: Misdeed can also mean something naughty or wicked that a person has done.
fact: Phrases you may see are past misdeeds, punished for his misdeeds, and own up to a misdeed.
fact: In church life, confession is a time to admit misdeeds and ask for forgiveness.
exercise: «The thief was punished for his misdeeds.» What does misdeeds mean? | Presents | Good deeds | *Wrong actions | Long walks
exercise: «Sam owned up to his misdeed and said sorry.» What is a misdeed? | A type of sweet | Something kind you did for a friend | *A wrong or bad action | A game played at school
exercise: Which word means a wrong or bad action? | garden | castle | *misdeed | kite
test: In the story, the villain was punished for his misdeeds. Misdeeds here means | Party games | Kind acts | *Wrong or bad actions | Lost keys
test: What does mis- mean at the start of misdeed? | *Wrong | Again | Happy | Many
exam: Which sentence uses misdeed well? | Ella ate a sandwich for her lunch at school. | *Ella said sorry for her misdeed and promised never to do it again. | The sky was blue and the sun was warm. | We went to the park to play football after tea.
